A||||4||88formula||Pictures of my Formula and info on Borla Exhaust||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||04-09-2000||11:04 PM||||I finally got pictures of my Formula. This Formula has 50,000 miles on it right now and it had 48200 miles when I bought it in the fall of 1999. <P>Right now I am in the process of doing some subtle modifications. These include the following <P>(1) Borla exhaust with the chrome tips bought from Dason auto in Californa for $525. <BR>(2) Porting the exhaust manifolds (pulled then off because they had loose bolts and leaked).<BR>(3) Sending the manifolds along with the crossover pipe to Jet Hot to get coated inside and out.<BR>(4) Crane Cams Gold Race Roller Rockers $319 from Performance Automotive Warehouse for the ultimate in valve train control (cool SOUND, more HP, better gas mileage, cooler running, and just plain more efficient).<BR>(5) Strip corrosion off wheel rims and clear coat.<P>The modifications I have already done are,<BR>(1) Underdrive pulley<BR>(2) Rodney Dickmans leather boot and shifter rebuild kit (very nice stuff and great top-notch quality at a great price)<BR>(3) Accel coil.<P>My formula,  <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233031" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233031</A> <BR>Interior,  <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233022" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233022</A> <BR>and, <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233009" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233009</A> <BR>THE BORLA EXHAUST EVERYONE WANTS. You cant see the Borla name on the muffler because of the glare from the flash and the pipe in the back were the catalytic converter goes is a cheap piece from the fiero store (you may notice no mandrel). <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233085" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233085</A> <BR>Engine compartment, <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233095" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233095</A> <BR>The back of what those low riding rice burning fart cans will soon see (at the track), <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233090" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233090</A>  <BR>I used to have an 87 coupe that I have sold to my brother. He is doing some modifications as well, which are,<BR>(1) Vented brake rotor kit from the Fiero Store <BR>(2) New heat coated (inside and out) exhaust manifold from the Fiero Store. The old one broke at the o2 sensor when I tried to take the o2 sensor off (cheap thing). <BR>(3) Rear swaybar kit from the Fiero Store<BR>His coupe,http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233077<BR>His interior,   <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233072" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=588057&a=4294470&p=19233072</A> <P>You can get the Borla exhaust at Dason Auto Concepts Inc. 908 W. Hyde Park Blvd Inglewwod, CA 90302<BR>Phone (310) 677-7185<BR>Fax (310) 677-2630 <BR>This is where I got mine. It was the last one on the shelf but he said he could order some more one at a time.<BR>||||reg||1
